WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.450
"Tokyo 7th Prison"

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.950
You look a little different than usual today.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.410
I've dressed up like a
yakuza wife for the occasion.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.790
Thanks for coming.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.950
I thought you'd all forgotten about me.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.160
I'm sorry it took so long.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.700
It was hard to get permission
to cross the ward border.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.040
What happened to your face?

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.950
I tripped, is what the records say.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.500
That's ridiculous!

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.080
You wouldn't get a bruise like that from a fall.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.250
It's nothing.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.540
You're such a worrywart, Watson.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.540
Of course I'm worried.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.000
You're still a kid!

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.290
The guys inside got to you, huh?

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.250
I demand to see the warden!

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.290
Quiet! Or I'll end the interview!

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.410
Just you try!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.830
I'll tell everyone that Warden Goro

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.830
Are you alone?

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:12.910
is a pervert who likes to wear

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.200
a woman's thong and has thick chest hair!

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.200
Yeah.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.200
I have people looking after me.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.200
Hey! Be quiet!

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.700
Hang in there.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:22.910
The people are calling you a hero.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.540
Thanks.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.910
But I killed a man.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.790
I have to atone for that.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:36.580
"Koyoru's Collection of Superstitions"

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.290
This is a present from Sherlock.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.580
Nobody would want to read this but Sherlock!

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.830
Think about what somebody
else might want to read--

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.870
"First Moonlit Night"

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.080
Hey, what were you trying to do?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.700
I'm sorry! My mom and dad are sick! So...

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:42.160
I don't care if your father broke every
bone in his body and is at death's door

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.160
or if your mother has stage 4 cancer.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.790
It's not my problem.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.790
You piece of shit four-eyes smarty-pants!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.160
Dummy! Jerk-face!

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.660
I'm so worried.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.910
About what?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.410
Moriarty, of course.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.540
I'm not worried.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.410
Why not? Your friend is--

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.040
Hello?

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.160
Brother?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.910
You don't have the right to call me brother.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.870
Of course. Sorry.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.370
What do you want, Mycroft?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:40.790
Ward Mayor Moran is not
popular on the East Side.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.410
I'm here to ask Mrs. Hudson to help
gather votes, and stopped in.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.160
The election's not for another six months.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.950
Elections aren't as simple
as you think they are.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.870
Even a year isn't enough.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.660
I'll be coming to the East Side
constantly from now on.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.370
Well, you don't need to come see me.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.910
Leave.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.620
Don't talk that way when he
was nice enough to come visit.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.120
I'm going to use your bathroom.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.950
Go ahead.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.500
This one's the bathroom.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.040
Of course.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.830
I'll make some coffee.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.450
Why not be a little nicer?

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:47.830
We'll be talking to him a lot about Moriarty.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:59.080
By the way, I went to see
Moriarty--I mean, James.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.450
He was being abused.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.660
We've heard the same reports.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.160
We're doing all we can.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.870
"Sherlock"

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.330
That's the sign that a new job's come in.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.290
I'm not going this time.

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.290
No, let's do it.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.290
If we're not doing something,
we'll just be thinking about Moriarty.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.870
So did you contact the police?

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.370
Of course!

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.950
"Client"

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.950
But they won't do a thing!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.620
It's been three days since he went missing!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.290
My brother must have been killed!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.750
Calm down.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.160
I'm sorry.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:44.540
What happened?

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:50.410
My brother went to Kooriyama in
Fukushima Prefecture to fish with a friend.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.950
But only the friend returned.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:57.200
The friend said they went
bass fishing in different boats,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.250
and my brother never came back.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.500
The friend killed him! I know it!

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.370
That's not enough to say he was murdered...

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.080
Did they go fishing in Asakanuma?

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.790
H-Huh? Yes.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.200
How did you know?

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:19.080
And your brother was in an illicit
relationship with the friend's wife.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.290
How did you know?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:25.450
It's just like <i>Koheiji the Living</i> !

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.290
What do you mean?

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:29.000
I'm taking the job!

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.790
Okay...

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.910
Hey, we have to do this in order!

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:34.790
Shut up!

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:38.410
There's no time for orders here, dork!

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.870
Hey, old man! You look pretty happy!

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.040
He's acting pretty happy,

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.290
but I'm sure he's really down

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:45.370
Of course! How could I not be,

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.750
over what happened with Moriarty.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:48.540
given the circumstances?

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.540
So when did you go to work

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.370
for Ward Mayor Moran, brother?

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:54.540
I told you that you don't have
the right to call me brother.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.040
Sorry.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.250
I've been his personal secretary for five years.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:05.410
Then you've known the
two of them for a long time.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:09.000
The Holmes family is one of the
West Side's oldest and most established.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.700
Many geniuses have come from our line.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.540
Sherlock's no exception.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.540
"#1 Sherlock Holmes"

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:24.000
But one day he left the house,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.370
saying he was dying of boredom each day.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:37.000
And he ended up here in Kabukicho.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:37.000
"Kabukicho 221st Avenue"

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.450
The disorder in this town must
have felt like freedom to him.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.950
"Koheiji the Living"

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:06.660
I came to get him, after a while,
but he said some strange nonsense,

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:10.950
"Koheiji the Living" "Lamphouse Koyoru"

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:10.950
about the human heart being impossible
to calculate, and thus interesting.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:16.410
Get out of here, you broke loser!

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.620
And it was none other than

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.410
Koheiji looking at us

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.660
with the shadow of the
lamp cast across his face...

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.660
Does Koheiji intend to kill me?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:30.410
No idea. I'm not thinking about that.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.620
I'm sure it'll go well.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:40.330
Hey, you're a scary woman...
You're the one who made them kill Koheiji!

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.040
Well, would you look at that.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.450
A storyteller!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.950
Wait... Wait!

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.750
Walk a little slower, so I can keep up!

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:58.080
I'm in a hurry! A hurry!

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:04.160
I've spent five years watching you
since Mrs. Hudson asked me to.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.950
But all you ever do is copy others.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.660
I've never seen your own <i>rakugo</i> .

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.950
Something's missing.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.370
"Something" tells me nothing.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:19.200
You'll just have to find out
what it is yourself.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:27.540
I think it's best if you not come back.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.290
Wait... Wait!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:47.620
Walk a little slower, so I can keep up!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.200
I'm in a hurry! A hurry!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.410
That's <i>Koheiji the Living</i> , right?

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.580
The tempo, the rhythm, the pauses...

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.290
You were doing Master
Koyoru's version, right?

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.250
Here.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.950
But you can't make a living
off <i>rakugo</i> like that.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:18.370
The characters seem flat. Not alive.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:24.790
It's probably because you
don't have a heart yourself.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:30.080
But because you don't have a heart,
you want to know what a heart is.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:37.620
So you're doing <i>rakugo</i>
to find a clue to what it is, huh?

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.700
I like your <i>rakugo</i> .

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.330
I'm hungry!

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.790
Feed me something.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.580
You said you were a bartender, right?

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:55.830
Let's go.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.450
So that's what I need.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:11.620
So you're saying you want me
to find the real criminal

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:14.620
to help prove your son's innocence.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.750
Leave it to me!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.080
I've got a whole stable of genius detectives.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.950
I'll solve the case in an instant.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:25.370
Hey, is this a detective agency, too?

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.620
Let me start by explaining

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.370
how our ranking systems work.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.290
It's stupid.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.290
I recommend you go with the S rank

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.200
But it might be more fun
than being a bartender.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.200
with bonus, and...

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.200
Coming up with deductions and stuff.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:34.660
There's no need to even bother deducting.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.700
The criminal is the son.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.040
What?

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.580
What did you say?

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:45.330
Your son said it was just 5,000,000 yen, right?

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.330
Yes, why?

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.540
Only the person who stole it
would know the exact number.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.580
Your son and one of his delinquent buddies

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:57.540
put on an act to get money from Daddy.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.000
That little shit!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.080
Bye!

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.870
Make sure to send the money!

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.160
Well done.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.870
Why not be a detective?

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:19.250
Hatred, joy, sorrow, all strong
enough to cause crimes.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:23.500
Wouldn't you be exposed to all
different kinds of human hearts?

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:27.410
That's what you wanted
to find in <i>rakugo</i> , right?

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:30.950
I know.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.250
Why not do it together?

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:33.250
Do what?

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.200
Dork. I mean do what detectives do,
make deductions, right?

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.870
Make it into a <i>rakugo</i> !

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:44.410
I mean mystery-solving <i>rakugo</i> !

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:49.580
And that's how he ended up here.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.450
So that's how it got started.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:55.790
I thought they made a strange pair.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.370
But it feels like

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:59.080
Yes... I knew it.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:01.500
the two of them are alike somehow.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.500
Knew what?

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.580
That's enough.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:12.160
"Prisoner"

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.160
Let's go.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.910
Are you okay?

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:27.950
Isshiki- <i>san</i> ...

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:33.080
I'm sorry to make you keep
helping me out like this.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:36.120
You're a hero on the outside, after all.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.580
So the guards are willing
to let us use the medical room.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.580
You're out in a week, right?

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:49.200
I'll come visit.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.410
What's that?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:01.200
A friend who came to visit me
today gave it to me.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.450
A friend named Sherlock Holmes.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:13.250
I always felt I was missing something,
ever since I was young.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:18.160
It was my mom and my little sister Alex

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.160
James!

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:21.500
that filled that hole.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.000
Having the two of them by my side

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.700
was really what kept me going.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.700
Here's your hat!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.500
But...

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.700
Mistress! Mistress!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.870
Somebody come quick!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.830
Mom...

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.000
I can't believe this!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.830
Mistress!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:58.040
It's okay. Don't cry.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:01.910
Dad doesn't hate you.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:05.040
He's sad that Mom's gone.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.120
That's why.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:11.370
But he says I'm not normal. I'm creepy.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.700
We're twins, right?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:20.000
So I know you better than anybody.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:25.500
You're not creepy. You're just a normal boy.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:39.500
School's not fun?

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:43.410
Teachers who couldn't teach
if their lives depended on it.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:47.000
Students who are all pride and no brains.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.790
They're all fools.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.200
What?

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:54.830
James!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.830
Stop sitting in your room
and go out and play!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.580
I'm not a little kid...

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.450
Hey, why not go to the East Side?

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.410
The East Side?

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.870
I heard it's a dump.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:16.160
I never get to go outside, right?

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:19.160
So I think about a lot of things.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:23.000
About how there's so much
in this world I don't know about.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:27.160
And that the more I knew,
the more I'd come to love it.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:29.870
So I want you to...

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:33.120
To keep loving this world, too, right?

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:01.580
Is that man the one who filled
in the gaps in your heart?

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.330
No.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.950
When I heard his <i>rakugo</i> , I understood.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:13.540
He's like me. He's got a hole in his heart.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.000
Thank you!

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.410
You found another one!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.790
And so Sherlock's just nuts!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.450
Today he started slapping
this corpse and smelling it--

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:31.830
Stop it.

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.660
But...

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:37.330
He and I get along.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:43.620
You know, it's fun to listen to you
when you're having fun!

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:51.250
There's still any number of things
in this world we don't know about.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:54.830
So many people we don't know.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:58.620
And they're waiting to meet us.

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:02.370
That's a wonderful thing, isn't it?

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:09.040
So I want you to always
keep loving this world.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.450
Even after Alex left me,

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:21.290
Sherlock and the rest of the
row house were there for me.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:25.200
So I told myself I wasn't alone.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:30.580
But in the end...

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:35.950
...I'm alone again...

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.910
Don't worry.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.620
You're not alone.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:46.200
Isshiki, I told you he's my prey.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.450
Right?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:52.290
No, I was just treating his wounds...

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.120
No! Please!

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.290
Albert- <i>san</i> !

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.080
No!

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:08.830
Which means that the criminal is right
in front of us. It's the client himself.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:10.790
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:18.500
You killed your brother and tried to pin it
on the friend since he had no alibi.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.500
What's wrong with this guy?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.870
Hey, are you listening?

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:25.910
But the client said he was in his home
on the West Side all day, right?

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.330
The client smelled of <i>himeshaka</i> .

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:36.250
Also called " <i>hanakatsumi</i> ," it's a flower
that only blooms in Asakanuma.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:46.040
Give yourself up, Kohada.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.450
How is a criminal with a good alibi like

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.410
Thought you could fool us

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:53.830
with a fake job, huh?

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.500
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:57.040
the ice cream you buy on a bullet train?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.250
You're gonna pay for
making me do all that work!

00:20:57.040 --> 00:21:02.120
It's hard to get either of them to melt.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:04.830
You didn't do anything!

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.830
That's all the time we have for today.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:10.290
Brilliant as ever, my brother.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:15.870
Um, by the way, is there
any connection between

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:21.790
Sherlock's knowing Moriarty and
you working for Moran, brother?

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.540
It's a coincidence.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:26.160
Just a coincidence.

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:11.080
Tsujimoto- <i>san</i> , how is Isshiki- <i>san</i> ?

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:13.330
He left this morning.

00:23:13.330 --> 00:23:16.700
But he wasn't supposed to leave for a week.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:21.120
He's headed to the hospital after
what Albert- <i>san</i> and his buddies did.

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:24.750
That got him out of here a week early.

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.040
Assuming he survives.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:35.040
Do you know how he
wound up here to begin with?

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.910
Tried to poison his wife, I heard.

00:23:37.910 --> 00:23:41.200
But it was unintentional, he said.

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:43.120
I don't know about that.

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:05.040
"Get Back Your Melon Heart"

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:05.040
A job for me? But I'm not
a detective anymore...

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.000
"Jack and the Moran Family"
"It was James that Moran really wanted dead.
Alexandra died in his place."
